## Why This Is Asked
Real-world need for a multi-tenant policy engine to enforce per-tenant constraints without downtime.

## Key Concepts
- Policy-as-code and versioning
- Per-tenant gating and feature flags
- Zero-downtime updates, revocation, and rollback
- Observability and auditing for policy changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-policy check
function checkPolicy(tenant, request) {
  const p = policyStore.get(tenant);
  if (!p) return false;
  if (request.model_version !== p.allowedModel) return false;
  if (!p.allowedRegions.includes(request.region)) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test policy revocation safety under traffic spikes?
- How would you handle cross-region policy replication and consistency?

## Why This Is Asked
Explains how to add observability and robust failure handling in a real API, a common beginner hurdle as systems scale.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed tracing, metrics, circuit breakers
- Idempotency and retry strategies
- Canary rollout and failover testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight circuit-breaker sketch
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold=5, windowMs=60000) { this.failures=0; this.threshold=threshold; this.open=false; }
  recordFailure(){ this.failures++; if(this.failures>this.threshold){ this.open=true; setTimeout(()=>{ this.open=false; this.failures=0; }, 30000);} }
  canProceed(){ return !this.open; }
}
```

